 ## Overview
-Texture Slabs is a volume rendering technique that loads 3D density data into the graphics card's texture map memory, treating the volume as a series of slabs between slices [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from standard ray casting by enabling the pre-integration of the volume rendering integral, allowing for efficient accumulation of color and opacity along rays [S1, S2, unofficial].
